            {
              "_key": "c4l2k009",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k009s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The winners had fundamentals behind them. The pandemic drove global demand for medicines, and the shift to remote work and digital everything drove a boom in technology spending. Meanwhile, PSU banks were still paying for the bad loan cycle, and public sector companies were out of favour.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k010",
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k010st1",
                  "label": "India's pharma exports, FY21",
                  "value": "US$24.44 billion",
                  "context": "Up about 18% in the pandemic year, a record at the time"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k010st2",
                  "label": "Infosys revenue growth, FY22",
                  "value": "19.7%",
                  "context": "Constant currency; its fastest growth in 11 years"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k010st3",
                  "label": "PSU banks' combined result, FY19",
                  "value": "₹66,636 crore loss",
                  "context": "Followed by a ₹25,941 crore loss in FY20"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k011",
              "_type": "callout",
              "type": "insight",
              "text": "Metals were actually the second-best performer of Act 1, rising on a global commodity boom. A rotation story is always a simplification. The value of a case study is not that it fits neatly, but that it shows how leadership changes and what signals appeared along the way."
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k012",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k012s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The Turn: Late 2021 to 2022",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k013",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k013s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The rotation did not happen on a single day. Pharma's relative strength had already peaked in September 2020, as the pandemic demand spike faded and US generic pricing pressure returned. IT kept leading for another fifteen months, then peaked at the end of 2021. Several signals lined up around that turn.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k014",
              "_type": "timeline",
              "title": "Signals Around the Turn",
              "events": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k014ev1",
                  "date": "FY21",
                  "title": "PSU banks return to profit",
                  "description": "After five straight years of losses, public sector banks posted a combined net profit of ₹31,820 crore, helped by recoveries and falling bad loans. The fundamental turn came well before the share prices re-rated."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k014ev2",
                  "date": "Dec 2021",
                  "title": "IT relative strength peaks",
                  "description": "After a spectacular run on digital demand and record growth, IT's outperformance stopped expanding as valuations stretched and expectations peaked."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k014ev3",
                  "date": "May 2022",
                  "title": "RBI starts hiking",
                  "description": "The repo rate began its 250 bps climb. Lesson 2.3 showed banks with fast-repricing loans benefit early in a hiking cycle."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k014ev4",
                  "date": "2022",
                  "title": "Global tech slowdown",
                  "description": "Rising US interest rates hit technology spending. IT relative strength fell sharply through 2022."
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k014ev5",
                  "date": "Dec 2022",
                  "title": "PSU banks cross above 100",
                  "description": "PSU bank relative strength climbed back above its December 2019 level, confirming the leadership change in price."
                }
              ]
            },
            {
