            {
              "_key": "c4l2k017",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k017s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "The new leaders were almost the mirror image of Act 1. The Nifty CPSE index, whose largest constituents in August 2026 were NTPC, Bharat Electronics, ONGC, Coal India, and Power Grid, returned +222.1%. PSU banks returned +170.9%. IT, the star of Act 1, managed just +9.3% while the Nifty 50 rose +50.9%.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k018",
              "_type": "statGrid",
              "stats": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k018st1",
                  "label": "Central govt capex, actual",
                  "value": "₹4.3 to ₹10.5 lakh crore",
                  "context": "FY21 to FY25, as reported from budget documents"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k018st2",
                  "label": "PSU banks' net profit",
                  "value": "₹1.41 lakh crore to ₹1.78 lakh crore",
                  "context": "FY24 to FY25, a record; ₹1.98 lakh crore in FY26"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k018st3",
                  "label": "PSU banks' gross NPAs",
                  "value": "14.58% to 1.93%",
                  "context": "FY18 peak to March 2026"
                },
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k018st4",
                  "label": "Infosys revenue growth",
                  "value": "1.4% (FY24), 4.2% (FY25)",
                  "context": "Constant currency, down from 19.7% in FY22"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k019",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "normal",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k019s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "Again, the price moves tracked fundamentals. Government capex more than doubled, lifting order books for public sector engineering, power, and defence companies. India's defence exports reached a record ₹23,622 crore in FY25. PSU bank profits went from heavy losses to records as bad loans shrank. And IT's growth slowed to low single digits as global tech spending cooled.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "_key": "c4l2k020",
              "_type": "block",
              "style": "h2",
              "markDefs": [],
              "children": [
                {
                  "_key": "c4l2k020s1",
                  "_type": "span",
                  "text": "What Happened Next",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
